        "answer": {
          "short": "$y^2+5y+9$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2y+3)(y+2)&=2y^2+4y+3y+6\\\\&=2y^2+7y+6\\\\(y-1)(y+3)&=y^2+3y-y-3\\\\&=y^2+2y-3\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubtract the second product, changing the sign of each term.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(2y+3)(y+2)-(y-1)(y+3)&=2y^2+7y+6-y^2-2y+3\\\\&=y^2+5y+9\\end{align*}$$",
